<address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>IEKI, TOSHIYA</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NAKAJIMA, YUUICHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TSUKUDA, AKIMITSU</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A polymer film characterized in that a Poisson's ratio of a width direction (TD) to a lengthwise direction (MD) of the film is less than 0.4, the film being excellent in size stability under a high tensile force and providing a high-capacity magnetic recording medium which is not susceptible to a reading error at a reproduction time and is excellent in electromagnetic transducing characteristics.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un film polymère se caractérisant en ce que le coefficient de Poisson, entre le sens de la largeur (TD) et le sens de la longueur (MD) du film, est inférieur à 0,4, en que sa stabilité dimensionnelle est excellente lorsqu'il est exposé à un effort de traction élevé et en qu'il constitue un support d'enregistrement magnétique de grande capacité, non sujet au risque d'erreur de lecture lors de la reproduction et présentant d'excellentes caractéristiques de transduction électromagnétique.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>